## The really strong composition

The software-supply-chain tools are no longer random micro-APIs:

```text
container/image
      │
      ▼
artifact.oci_platform.resolve
      │
      ▼
exact immutable digest
      │
      ▼
artifact.oci_referrers.discover
      │
      ├──── SBOM ───────► sbom.spdx.validate
      │                  sbom.cyclonedx.validate
      │                         │
      │                         ▼
      │                   sbom.vex.resolve
      │
      ├──── signature ───► artifact.sigstore.verify
      │
      ├──── attestation ─► artifact.intoto_attestation.verify
      │
      └──── receipt ─────► supplychain.scitt_receipt_verify
                              │
                              ▼
                    VERIFIED EVIDENCE PACKET
                              │
                              ▼
                         agent decision
```

That is much more interesting than “80 free APIs.”

TinyTools starts looking like a **deterministic evidence resolution layer**:

> **discover evidence → normalize evidence → verify evidence → compose evidence → let the agent reason over verified facts**

This is potentially a stronger identity than “stdlib for agents.”

